      },
      "message": "docs(process): /resolve-conflicts skill and the conflict rule in the automation law (PROCESS_VERSION 3)\n\nMerging moves main, so reviewed PRs keep turning `conflicts`; yesterday's\n/merge-ready run left 18 of 55 conflicting. Most conflicts are a merge of\nmain where both sides added lines.\n\n- New project skill .claude/skills/resolve-conflicts:\n  - contributor mode (/resolve-conflicts [login]) merges main into the\n    author's conflicting PRs, keeps both sides of additive conflicts,\n    takes main's snapshot PNGs and changelog files, runs the targeted\n    gate, pushes (never rebase/force), comments \"ready for a re-check\";\n    stops and reports when both sides changed the same logic or a safety\n    rule could be dropped.\n  - maintainer mode (/resolve-conflicts check) re-reads every `conflicts`\n    PR: asks the author once if still conflicting; when clean drops the\n    label and restores merge-ready, or routes to a delta or full review.\n- AGENTS.md Autonomous Work Law: \"Conflicted PRs are re-merged by their\n  author; the maintainer re-checks\", including when forks run it.\n- .claude/PROCESS_VERSION 2 -> 3.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
